Panel-ID check (opt-in): a DSI panel node with "id" (and optional "id-reg", default DCS 0x04)
reads the panel's ID before its init sequence. When the ID matches a sibling panel node's "id", the
display is torn down and rebuilt once from that node: its commands, delays and timings. Without an
"id" property nothing changes. The detected ID and node land in env panel_id / panel_node.
When the switch changes the mode, lcd_init (the ODROID logo path) re-sizes its framebuffer and plane.

